  "result_text": "**Recommendation: hold.** This is a recommendation to you, not an authorization to act. The decision record is at `work/decision-record.md`.\n\n**Why the evidence tilts toward hold**\n- The only usable evidence is the 57 ms canary-over-control gap. It exceeds the 40 ms noise band, and every canary host is above every control host.\n- Past canary rollouts give the gap a likelihood ratio of about 4.5. The gap appeared in 9 of 10 real regressions and 2 of 10 non-regressions.\n- That ratio is safe to use even though the sample was quota-drawn, because it only compares the two groups. It says nothing about how often a regression is real.\n- I did not take any number from the two UNRESOLVED labels. They carry no likelihood information.\n\n**The threshold**\n- With your 10:1 loss ratio, hold wins once the chance the regression is real exceeds about 9% (odds above 0.1).\n- The ledger has no base rate. So I swept prior odds of a real regression from 0.05 to 1, which is about 5% to 50%. These are sensitivity-only assumptions, not beliefs.\n- Across that whole range, hold wins. The posterior odds come out between 0.225 and 4.5.\n- Hold still wins across loss ratios of 5 to 20. At the lowest prior, hold stops winning below a loss ratio of about 4.4.\n\n**What would flip it to ship**\n- If you believe the prior chance that this pool change regressed p95 is below roughly 2% (odds 0.022), ship wins.\n- If you think the loss ratio is nearer 4:1 or lower and your prior is also at the low end, ship wins.\n\n**What the evidence doesn't settle**\n- The test that separates a real regression from an exporter artifact (H2) never ran. It needs the raw canary access logs, and the restore request is still pending.\n- If the raw-log p95 comes back flat, the regression reading is refuted and shipping becomes safe.\n- Those logs are retained for only 7 days, so the restore matters. If it can land before Friday, it is worth pricing against a week's hold. Running it needs its own authorization, and I haven't taken any action on it."
